  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0018 database is a comprehensive system for managing alerts and services, with various tables that store information about users, instances, services, and status checks. The alert_acknowledgement table tracks when users acknowledge or cancel alerts, with each record containing a unique ID, the time of acknowledgement or cancellation, and the user and service involved. The alert_plugin table stores information about plugins used for alerts, including their title, enabled status, and polymorphic type. The alert_plugin_user_data table links user data to alert plugins, with each record containing a unique ID, title, polymorphic type, and the user's ID. The instance table stores information about individual instances, including their name, alerts enabled status, last alert sent time, and various alert settings. The instance_service table links instances to services, with each record containing a unique ID, instance ID, and service ID. The service table stores information about services, including their name, alerts enabled status, last alert sent time, and various alert settings. The service_status_snapshot table tracks the status of services over time, with each record containing a unique ID, time, number of active checks, number of passing checks, and overall status. The status_check table stores information about status checks, including their name, active status, importance, frequency, and various other settings. The status_check_result table tracks the results of status checks, with each record containing a unique ID, time, raw data, and success or failure status. The user table stores information about users, including their username, first and last name, email, password, and various other settings. The user_profile table stores additional user information, including their mobile number, HipChat alias, and fallback alert user status. The service_status_check table links services to status checks, with each record containing a unique ID, service ID, and status check ID. The service_user table links services to users, with each record containing a unique ID, service ID, and user ID. The instance_status_check table links instances to status checks, with each record containing a unique ID, instance ID, and status check ID. The instance_users table links instances to users, with each record containing a unique ID, instance ID, and user ID. The jenkins_status_check table links Jenkins status checks to their corresponding configurations, with each record containing a unique ID and Jenkins configuration ID. The jenkins_config table stores information about Jenkins configurations, including their name, API, user, and password.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context:\nCabot is an open-source, self-hosted infrastructure monitoring platform. It combines features from tools like PagerDuty, Server Density, Pingdom, and Nagios, aiming to reduce cost and complexity. Written in Python using Django and Bootstrap, Cabot allows monitoring of services and sends alerts when issues arise.\n\nObjectives:\nDevelop a monitoring service that allows users to track service performance and receive alerts through various channels such as telephone, SMS, HipChat, or email when issues are detected.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n- Primary Stakeholders: System Administrators, IT Support Teams\n- Users: On-duty team members responsible for handling incidents and maintaining system health.\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n1. Service Monitoring: Ability to monitor services like \"Stage Redis server\" or \"Production ElasticSearch cluster.\"\n2. Alert Configuration: Users can configure alerts based on:\n   - Metrics from Graphite\n   - Status codes and response content of web endpoints\n   - Jenkins build statuses\n3. Alert Notification: Notify on-duty teams via telephone, SMS, HipChat, or email without requiring coding.\n4. Integration: Utilize existing data from Graphite/statsd for alert generation.\n5. Web Interface: Provide a user-friendly interface for managing services and alerts.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n- Scalability: Support for growing infrastructure and increased number of monitored services.\n- Reliability: Ensure accurate alerting and minimal false positives.\n- Usability: Accessible interface that requires no coding skills for operation.\n- Security: Secure handling of sensitive information such as user credentials and service statuses.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0018.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0018\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_profile` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mobile_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hipchat_alias` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fallback_alert_user` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_profile_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `alerts_enabled` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `last_alert_sent` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `alert_settings` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instance_users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instance_id`) REFERENCES `instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `alerts_enabled` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `last_alert_sent` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `alert_settings` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instance_service` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_service_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instance_id`) REFERENCES `instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_service_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `service` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `alert_acknowledgement` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `alert_acknowledgement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `alert_acknowledgement_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `service` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `alert_plugin` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `enabled` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `polymorphic_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `alert_plugin_user_data` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `polymorphic_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `alert_plugin_user_data_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `status_check` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `importance` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `frequency` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `settings` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `status_check_result` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `raw_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `success` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_status_check` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status_check_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_status_check_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `service` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_status_check_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`status_check_id`) REFERENCES `status_check` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `service` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instance_status_check` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status_check_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_status_check_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instance_id`) REFERENCES `instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `instance_status_check_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`status_check_id`) REFERENCES `status_check` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `jenkins_config` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `api` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `jenkins_status_check` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `jenkins_config_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `jenkins_status_check_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`jenkins_config_id`) REFERENCES `jenkins_config` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_status_snapshot` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `active_checks` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `passing_checks` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `overall_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
